{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"\\\"##### shell/notes.md #####\\\"; Get-Content -Raw 'shell\\\\notes.md'; \\\"##### shell/checks.json #####\\\"; Get-Content -Raw 'shell\\\\checks.json'; \\\"##### final-docs-glm-report.md #####\\\"; Get-Content -Raw 'final-docs-glm-report.md'\"","aggregated_output":"##### shell/notes.md #####\r\n# G1 lifecycle and DOM shell integration contract\n\nScope: W1 store, descriptors/session resources, legacy load lease and RingInspection DOM/CSS only. Existing staged versions remain staged; this work is unstaged. Shared scene, camera, lights, post, hero and ring sampler were not edited. No commit, push or deployment.\n\n## Runtime factory and readiness\n\n`StoryRuntime` adds exactly `readonly root: Object3D` and `readonly ready: Promise<void>` to the reviewed interface. `StoryDescriptor.create(session, ctx)` remains synchronous. It constructs an instance-owned root, returns the runtime immediately, and starts session-owned async fetch/parse work. Pass `session.signal` to requests. `ready` resolves after required assets have parsed; it does not mean shaders are compiled or the store is ready.\n\nW2 registers the real ring factory with `registerStory()`. Default ring metadata intentionally has no factory; the old scene remains its only adapter until W2 migration. No shaft descriptor, factory, trigger or static shaft substitute is installed. Shaft entry throws before acquiring ownership until a complete descriptor with required assets and a synchronous factory has been registered. Static shaft entry remains explicitly unavailable even with a registered runtime; it cannot fall through to the ring schematic. The shaft descriptor/static artwork remain later work. `getInspectionStory()` retains the immutable session metadata for DOM reads even if a factory registration is removed during teardown.\n\nIntegration order:\n\n1. Enter captures narrative context and creates `inspection.session`. Obtain the registered descriptor and synchronously create its runtime with that session. Factories own their resources through `session.own()`; disposal removes the root, releases owned resources and is idempotent.\n2. Call `setInspectionRuntime(runtime, session.id)`. It publishes the reference once and owns runtime disposal through the session. Repeating the assignment of the same instance is a no-op; assigning a stale instance disposes it and returns false. Mount `runtime.root` under the inspection world before awaiting `runtime.ready`. The runtime builds/fetches its assets under that instance-owned root; no camera writes.\n3. After `ready` resolves, check `session.current()`. Dispose stale results immediately and do not attach, compile, publish controls or acquire camera/render leases for them. Capture the epoch in every rejection handler and use `session.fail(error)` or `inspectionFailed(error, session.id)`.\n4. Publish `setInspectionStatus('compiling', session.id)`, apply lease-hidden narrative lighting, then perform the leased compile and 1px offscreen warm render, restoring renderer flags in `finally`. Check `session.current()` after each asynchronous step and again after warming. Only then call `setInspectionStatus('ready', session.id)`. Parsing alone cannot enable Play.\n5. A single integration-owned priority -10 driver advances and samples; CameraRig and geometry/application readers consume `inspection.runtime` imperatively. W1 only exports `advanceInspectionPlayhead(delta, stamp)` and installs no production caller. The original baseline ring scene advanced time itself; integration must delete that advancement when installing the new driver. Final source refresh observed W2's new caller in InspectionScene.tsx:25 and real ring factory registration. These are concurrent W2 edits, not W1 changes or shell verification. Audio is not installed by this leaf; seek/chapter/replay produce no audio events here.\n\n`inspection.playing` retains its compatibility setter so old ring/proof assignments update `userPlaying`; its getter derives effective playback from active/static/status/suspend/time. Frame advancement clamps delta to 0.05, rejects invalid/repeated/older stamps, holds at duration, and mutates scalars/telemetry without allocating or notifying on ordinary ticks. Chapter/end transitions alone notify. While hidden/context/error-suspended it advances neither time nor entryElapsed. Integration consumes `exiting` on its inactive frame; calling the exported advance function while inactive clears that one-frame marker.\n\n`createStorySession(kind, lifecycle)` takes explicit `{ id, current, fail }` callbacks supplied by the store. This dependency injection is the implementation clarification to the contract's one-argument sketch: session and story modules have no runtime store import/cycle. Owned resources are disposed once, stale owned results are disposed immediately, and cached borrows are reference-counted and released without disposing the cache.\n\n## DOM and restore\n\nPlay/Pause, Replay, labeled native seek and chapter commands use an epoch captured at render. Same-chapter paused seek does not broadcast; the DOM polls only visible time and updates the slider/output imperatively. Captions retain discrete status announcements. Ring has one chapter; chapter buttons appear only for registered multichapter stories. Entry is still the existing ring action; no shaft entry is exposed.\n\nThe dialog captures scroll coordinates, trigger, Lenis stop state, overflow, inert and chrome opacity in effect-local snapshots. It guards focusin/Tab/Escape, inerts newly inserted body siblings, restores original inert/opacity values and scroll, and resumes Lenis only if it was running. A disconnected trigger falls back to the current ring action, then the JGun chapter, then main/body; nonfocusable fallbacks retain a temporary tabindex until blur. Native focusable triggers retain their tab order. Return works while loading, compiling, failed and static. Retry cancels/restores the old epoch before opening a new paused session, with no delayed unscoped requestAnimationFrame callback.\n\n## Remaining W2 gates\n\nThis bounded implementation does not claim shared scene or full G1 acceptance. W2 owns migration of the original wall-clock 15s timeout and unscoped boundary error to captured sessions, replacing old ring advancement with the single driver, wiring the required compile/warm readiness sequence, holding narrative/render ownership through the end, and exact camera/render restoration. `createVisibleLoadDeadline(session, ms)` is unit-tested support: feed visible loading/compiling deltas only, resetting wall-time baselines on visibility changes; never feed hidden wall time. W1 made no shared scene edits; its isolated DOM proof does not verify W2's subsequent timeout/driver changes.\n\nFull ring runtime round trips, priority ordering, shader program stability, context-loss GL cleanup, resource census and opening regression belong to W2/integration. The DOM harness mounts the real shell without a canvas or CAD runtime. Its screenshots and report prove DOM behavior only. Fresh Anthropic-provider review remains pending; producer-side checks do not constitute that review.\n\nFinal producer evidence: 26/26 focused tests, scoped shell typecheck, repository typecheck and four DOM cases PASS. Two intermediate repository checks reported unused imports in integration-owned renderLease.ts:1; W2 corrected them before the final passing run. No changes to that file were made here. Parent separately reports 44 focused tests passing; W1's own rerun covers the exact four-file/26-test command in the shell gate. Nash owns the independent manufacturing runtime verifier and runtime/ evidence. Ring asset metadata pins the measured SHA-256 e5bff99439eb6655ea9eda3929fcca2f3e388b98c5742dcef95c371423c8fbd8; measured 1,798,620 bytes is under its 2 MiB limit. No asset was modified.\n\r\n##### shell/checks.json #####\r\n{\n  \"scope\": \"W1 lifecycle/store/DOM shell\",\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\n      \"command\": \"npx vitest run src/state/inspectionStore.test.ts src/scene/inspection/session.test.ts src/scene/inspection/story.test.ts src/scene/inspection/lifecycle.test.ts\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"filesPassed\": 4,\n      \"testsPassed\": 26,\n      \"lastRunStartAsPrinted\": \"14:27:59\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"npx tsc --noEmit -p project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/shell/tsconfig.shell.json\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"npm run typecheck\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"note\": \"Final repository run passed after concurrent integration owner corrected four unused imports; W1 did not edit shared source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"node project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/shell/verify-shell.mjs --url=http://localhost:5201\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"casesPassed\": 4,\n      \"cases\": [\"desktop\", \"narrow\", \"reduced-narrow\", \"poster-narrow\"],\n      \"details\": \"dom-report.json\",\n      \"scope\": \"Real DOM component in isolation; no scene/runtime/CAD fetch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"git diff --check -- src/state/inspectionStore.ts src/state/inspectionStore.test.ts src/scene/inspection/loadLease.ts src/components/RingInspection.tsx src/components/RingInspection.css\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"review\": \"Fresh Anthropic provider review pending\",\n  \"runtime\": \"W2 and Nash independent integration verification pending\",\n  \"stagedByW1\": false,\n  \"committedByW1\": false\n}\n\r\n##### final-docs-glm-report.md #####\r\nRelease file never arrived. Per the verification contract, I'm finishing with a preparation report and leaving all final edits pending — no files were modified this session.\n\n**Preparation report — JG-035 final docs (owned: PLAN.md, review-ledger.md, continuation-handoff-2026-10-06.md; banners TODO.md:3, project/README.md:3, project/work/INDEX.md:3)**\n\n`final-docs-release.md` stayed absent through 23:11:43 UTC despite polling past the 10-minute window, so the acceptance/status edits remain unapplied and nothing was inferred as released.\n\nVerified state, read from actual files this session:\n\n- **Shaft:** `runtime/shaft/contact-parent-run-{1,2}/report.json` each hold 16 cases, 12/12 gates (S1–S8, N1–N4) `pass:true`, 0 defects, 0 harness limitations; verifier `d26d491a…`, kinematics `2f78847d…`, desktop lite/narrow full. GLM correction review SHIP/SHIP.\n- **Lifecycle:** `parent-final-2026-10-06` = 14 cases, exactly 2 failures (reduced-motion desktop/narrow, 3 narrative CAD fetches each); V4/V6 unchecked.\n- **Static:** `static-parent-final` 4/4 pass, 0 failures; 16 WEBPs provenance-audited unchanged (CPU equivalence, 16/16 hashes, no rendered-execution claim).\n- **Gates:** core-assets D1–D5 checked (D4 SHIP; lite 0.053195 mm diagnostic failed, no waiver); camera C1–C4 checked; G0 mechanical GLM SHIP within named proxy limits; root GATES.md all seven unchecked.\n- **Parent checks:** 43 files/445 tests, build 703 modules (`index-DFY-biXM.js`/`SceneCanvas-CoJldWVG.js`), preview PID 33416 — recorded in continuation-checks, not re-run by me.\n\nPrepared edits (handoff top current-state section; PLAN table + new status-log entry; ledger acceptance update; three banner refreshes) keep V4 owner choice, owner visual acceptance, and root-gate decisions explicitly open; no commit/push/deploy occurred.\n\nNext action: parent drops `final-docs-release.md`; I re-read affected files, apply within minutes, and verify every new link plus the scoped diff.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
